{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018wWysisegaD3Sb9fxxv5PW","type":"tool_result","content":"# Contributing to Rich\n\nThis project welcomes contributions in the form of Pull Requests.\nFor clear bug-fixes / typos etc. just submit a PR.\nFor new features or if there is any doubt in how to fix a bug, you might want\nto open an issue prior to starting work, or email willmcgugan+rich@gmail.com\nto discuss it first.\n\nSee also [AI_POLICY.md](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/AI_POLICY.md) if you will be using AI.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n---\n\n## AI use in issues, and the triage bot\n\n*Added for the triage-agent sandbox; applies to everyone who opens an issue.*\n\nRich receives a growing number of AI-written issues and pull requests, and new\nissues are now first triaged by an automated agent. These rules apply to all\ncontributors, whether or not you use AI yourself.\n\n### If you use AI to write an issue\n\n1. **Say so.** Add a line such as `AI-assisted: drafted with <tool>` at the end.\n2. **Include a minimal reproducible example you ran yourself**, with its actual\n   output, your Rich version and platform (`python -m rich.diagnose`). A bug report\n   without a runnable example is labelled `more information needed`, however long\n   its analysis.\n3. **Feature requests still go to [Discussions](https://github.com/textualize/rich/discussions) first**,\n   as the feature template says. An AI-written proposal does not change that.\n4. Pull requests follow [AI_POLICY.md](AI_POLICY.md): fill in the template,\n   name the agent you used, and link an issue or discussion where a maintainer\n   approved the approach.\n\n### What the triage bot does and does not do\n\n- It runs once when an issue is opened. It may add up to three labels from\n  `bug`, `enhancement`, `question`, `documentation`, `duplicate`, `invalid`,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe720889-b668-47e2-89ff-10fe8524294d","uuid":"4